From b4e342471930c65ba0f4cfe025300ba8cb4e3029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wizard1209 <wizard1209@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 11:38:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(models): preserve l2_account GraphQL field, FK
 relation -> account

The A2 FK rename moved the column l2_account -> l2_account_id, a breaking
GraphQL shape change. Restore the old API: name the FK column l2_account
again (source_field) and call the relation field `account` instead, so the
relation name no longer collides with the column name (the collision broke
refresh_from_db before). Mirrors the existing ticket/ticket_hash pattern.

Result: GraphQL exposes the scalar `l2_account` exactly as before (string ==
origin), plus a new `account` object relation to L2Account (alias/kind).
Raw FK accessor is account_id; matcher and handlers updated accordingly.
Verified: l2_account column holds the origin value, matching unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
